      "scope": "Three or more fresh runs of the actual previously timed direct-counting C/Rust/fwp binaries, on the matching native architecture. GNU time records whole-process peak RSS in KiB, including startup, output and shutdown. These separate memory runs are excluded from the timing comparison; RSS includes shared code/libraries and has page/accounting granularity. Separate instrumented GCC O2 builds of saved fwp C count managed requests, retains and peak/final charged bytes after constant initialization through cleanup. They exclude raw buffers, allocator metadata, stacks and libc. A single injected 16-byte leaf allocation must be detected. No C/Rust allocator-call count or peak-RSS improvement over older fwp is claimed."
